 "院本": "دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (A composition, normally in prose, telling a story and intended to be represented) / دْرَامَا, مَسْرَحِيَّة (Theatrical plays in general.)  [drama]",
 "院長": "مُدِير, مُدِيرَة (One who directs; the person in charge of managing a department or directorate (e)  [director (of a hospital, institution, academy, etc.)]",
 "陣": "[battle formation] / مُخَيِّم (An outdoor place acting as temporary accommodation in tents or other simple stru)  [camp] / مَجْمُوعَة, جَمَاعَة (A number of things or persons being in some relation to one another.)  [group] / حَرْب (conflict involving organized use of arms) / مُحَارَبَة (conflict involving organized use of arms) / حرب (conflict involving organized use of arms) / حرب (conflict involving organized use of arms) / حَرْب (conflict involving organized use of arms) / حَارَبَ, شَنَّ حَرْبًا (To engage in conflict (may be followed by \"with\" to specify the foe).)  [war]",
 "陣々": "[each encampment] / قَوِيّ (Capable of producing great physical force.) / مَنِيع, مَتِيْن (Capable of withstanding great physical force.) / قَوِيّ, راسِخ (Determined; unyielding.) / شَدِيْد, قَوْيّ (Highly stimulating to the senses.) / شَدِيْد (Having an offensive or intense odor or flavor.) / حَادّ, ثَقِيْل (Having a high concentration of an essential or active ingredient.) / بِقُوَّة (In a strong manner.)  [strong (wind)] / مُتَقَطِّع (Stopping and starting, occurring, or presenting at intervals; coming after a par) / مَوْسِمِيّ (Existing only for certain seasons; that is, being dry for part of the year.)  [intermittent]",
 "陣営": "مُخَيِّم (An outdoor place acting as temporary accommodation in tents or other simple stru)  [camp (supporters of a doctrine, party, etc.)]\nمثال: クリントン陣営は、両州でオバマが取った白人票を取り崩そうと必死になった。\n→ The Clinton camp became desperate to eliminate the white votes Obama had got in both states. / مَحَلَّة, مُخَيَّم (A place where people (such as displaced people, soldiers, or travellers) encamp,)  [encampment]\norig. meaning",
 "陣地": "مَحَلَّة, مُخَيَّم (A place where people (such as displaced people, soldiers, or travellers) encamp,)  [encampment]\nمثال: 敵が守っている陣地はたいへん重要なので、その陣地を守るために敵はあくまで戦う。\n→ The position held by the enemy is so important they will fight to the bitter end to hold it. / جَانِب (A bounding straight edge of a two-dimensional shape.) / جَانِب (One half (left or right, top or bottom, front or back, etc.) of something or som) / صَفْحَة (One surface of a sheet of paper (used instead of \"page\", which can mean one or b)  [side]",
 "陣容": "[battle formation ; battle array] / تَشْكِيلَة (Collectively, the members of a team.)  [lineup (of a team, etc.)]",
